         <entry xml:id="istatniyot-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">איסטטניות</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾysṭṭnywt</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">ʾisṭaṭniyyot</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">adjective</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">f.</gram>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="istatniyot-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>seditious, quarrelsome</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>στασιωτεία</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ר' יהושע בר נחמיה אמר אף 
                     <app>
                        <lem>איסטטניות</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#V K">אוסטטניות</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1 Ox1">אסטטניות</rdg>
                     </app> ודבריניות, 
                     <app>
                        <lem>איסטטניות</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1 Ox1 Ox2">אסטטניות</rdg>
                     </app> ותאמר שרי אל אברם חמסי עליך</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">45,5</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 453: 2</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Yehosuaʿ bar Neḥemya said: They [the women] are also querulous and talkative; querulous [as it is stated]: And Sarai said unto Abram: My wrong be upon thee (Gen 16,5).</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">DtnR Ki-Teṣeʾ 6,11</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">איסטסוניות</term>) [<bibl type="modern">Liebermann 106</bibl>: <term xml:lang="jpa">איסטסניות</term>]; <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 79 [22c: 42]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אוסטטניות</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>According to <bibl type="modern">AC I 173a</bibl> (and Krauss) GenR shall be emended to <term xml:lang="jpa">אסטסיאנות</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭsyʾnwt</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">ʾasṭasianot</term> corresponding to Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">στασιώτης</term> or Lt. seditiosa. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 121a</bibl> interprets GenR as f. sg. <term xml:lang="jpa">אסטסיאנית</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭsyʾnyt</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">ʾisṭasianit</term> (while the parallel in DtnR is pl.) tracing back to Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">στασιώδης</term>; <bibl type="modern">Levy I 119a</bibl> suggests for the GenR reading Lat. stationalis, Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ἄστατος</term> or Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ἀσταθής</term>. <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 55a</bibl> retains the GenR reading and interprets it as a derivation from the Sem. root <term xml:lang="jpa">סטן</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">SṬN</term>. <bibl type="modern">Fürst 62</bibl> explains the GenR reading as Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">στασιάζων</term>. To be distinguished from <term xml:lang="jpa">אסטטית</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭṭyt</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">asṭaṭit</term> (<bibl type="ancient">mMak 1,5</bibl>), cf. <bibl type="modern">Heijmanns (2013) 27-28</bibl>. Cf. Syr. <term xml:lang="syc">ܐܣܛܣܝܢܐ</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭsynʾ</term> (<bibl type="modern">Sokoloff, SL 70a</bibl>).</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>81b</citedRange></bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
